      <revisionDesc>
          <change when="2025-01-25T18:47:10-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Finalized - done</change>
          <change when="2025-01-25T10:40:50-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Vote - Accept-Straight-to-Finalization - 6 πλοῖ[ο]ν̣ [τέ]ως is better than πλοῖ[ον ἁπλ]ῶς, but there is no guarantee about the adverb; add question mark || lin11 ἀπειλοῦντες is good || lin17 Ed. suggests ἀ̣μ̣ε̣λ̣εί̣ᾳ̣, but α̣ is difficult; ἐ̣μ̣[μ]ε[λ]εί̣α̣ suggests a single addressee and of much higher rank than a boethos.</change>
          <change when="2024-12-21T20:20:25-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Submit - Corrections in lines 6 and 11.</change>
          <change when="2024-12-21T20:18:36-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - In l. 6 ἁπλ]ῶς: the lacuna is not as wide as to accommodate both πλοῖ[ον and ἁπλ]ῶς. A simpler and shorter solution is τέ]ως μὴ θέλοντες ποιῆσαι ἄνευ ὕβρεως ('until now not wanting to do it without abuse'). In l. 11 ἀπειλοῦντες is written in full. In l. 15 ἐνέγκοντες =&gt; ἐνεγκόντες. In l. 17, I haven't added it but ἐ̣μ̣[μ]ε[λ]εί̣α̣ is a possibility, the alpha being the most difficult to justify. </change>
